  Adrenaline
    From "Adrenaline - Panic Counters Tiredness", Steam Workshop 2807001835.
    Stated terms: MIT, declared by the author in the mod description.

    Bundled: no files. The implementation was written for this project, because
    the original reads and writes fatigue through methods build 42 removed.

    Taken: the mechanic and its balance values, meaning the absorption caps per
    panic level, the rates and the crash multiplier. Those numbers are the
    author's judgement rather than ours, and MIT covers their reuse.

    The mod ships no licence file and names no author in mod.info, so no
    copyright line is reproduced here. The Workshop page above identifies the
    author.

  Ammo and Magazine Icons
    Workshop 1904952813, by falcon33jp
    Stated terms: none.

    Bundled: twelve inventory icons for ammo boxes and magazines. Build 42
    draws five handgun ammo boxes with one icon, three rifle boxes with
    another and three pistol magazines with a third, so these give each item
    its own. Artwork cannot be reimplemented from a description, so unlike the
    rest of this project these files are the originals.

    Not taken: the loose ammo icons and every world model. Vanilla's are fine.
    The code that applies them was written for this project.

  Cloth Recycling and DIY Workbooks
    From "Def's Long Term Survival", Steam Workshop 1962914415, by DefbeatCZ.
    Stated terms: MIT. The Workshop download carries no licence file; the licence
    is in the GitHub repository the mod's own mod.info points at,
    https://github.com/DefbeatCZ/DefsLTS, as Copyright (c) 2020 DefbeatCZ.

    Bundled: no files. Every recipe in that mod is build 41 syntax, which build 42
    replaced outright, so nothing there could be carried across even had it been
