  Lockpicking
    From "Lockpicking. Just. Lockpicking.", Steam Workshop 2056238799.
    Original by FMJ, updated for IWBUMS by MeTaLAnGeR, streamlined and fixed by
    Oh God Spiders No.
    Stated terms: none published with the mod. Included on the say so of this
    project's author, who confirmed permission to build on it.

    Bundled: four inventory icons and two sound files, the lockpicking loop and
    the window being forced. Artwork and audio cannot be rewritten from a
    description.

    Taken: the design and its numbers. The chance to pick a lock, the timings,
    which traits move them and by how much, the two rolls that stick or snap a
    pick, and where the manuals spawn are all the original's judgement.

    Rewritten for this project: everything that touched an api. Build 42 deleted
    TraitFactory and ProfessionFactory outright and will not take a trait from a
    mod at all, so the original's Nimble Fingers is gone and what it gave now
    rides on the burglar profession. The build 41 recipe format is gone, so all
    three recipes are craftRecipe blocks. Thirty nine
    calls to HasTrait took a string, which build 42 no longer accepts, and two of
    the traits they named, Lucky and Unlucky, no longer exist. Four of the five
    sounds it played have been retired from the base game and are replaced with
    vanilla ones that survive.

    Added here: where the hairpin spawns. The original defined a raw hairpin but
    never put one in a loot table, and build 42 has none of its own, so the
    recipe that bends one into a pick had nothing to work from.

    Not taken: its bundled copy of ItemTweaker, and its Necroforge support file.

  Moodle Quarters
    From "Moodle Quarters", Steam Workshop 2854030563, by DahakaMVl.
    Stated terms: explicit permission, given by the author in writing on the
    mod's Workshop page: "Feel free to use it in your QoL pack."

    Bundled: forty eight plate textures, six sizes by two sets by four levels.
    They are the author's build 41 artwork scaled up to the sizes build 42 uses,
    generated by tools/generate_plates.py in the upstream repository. The shape,
    the hard one pixel outline and the colours are the whole mod, so none of the
    three is redrawn or recomputed here.

    Also bundled: the lua that draws the stack. Build 41 shipped this mod as a
    texture pack, which build 42 made impossible by loading one background per
    size and tinting it by level, so the level shapes have to be drawn by the
    mod. That build 42 support was written by this project's author, offered
    upstream as a pull request and merged, so the file here and the file in the
    author's repository are deliberately the same file.

    This project's copy stands down entirely when the standalone mod is present,
    because both replace the same vanilla panel.

